* /**
*  * @file GIT.SENT
*  * @version 1.0
*  */
* GIT.SENT(s) — s = the current verb sentence, portably: mvx reads SENTENCE(),
* UniData reads @SENTENCE.  Handlers call this so the one platform difference in
* fetching the sentence lives in a single place.
SUBROUTINE GIT.SENT(S)
$INCLUDE BP.INC PLATFORM.H
* In machine mode the verb has already rewritten the sentence with its own flag
* removed, and left it here — so handlers parse exactly what they would have
* seen without the flag, and none of them has to know the mode exists.
      COMMON /GITMACH/ GMACH, GSENT
      IF GSENT # "" THEN
         S = GSENT
         RETURN
      END
$IFDEF MVX
   S = TRIM(SENTENCE())
$ELSE
   S = TRIM(@SENTENCE)
$ENDIF
RETURN